<title>USA: Hemagen gets FDA okay to sell Lupus test.</title>
<headline>Hemagen gets FDA okay to sell Lupus test.</headline>
<dateline>WALTHAM, Mass. 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hemagen Diagnostics Inc said Tuesday the Food and Drug Administration had cleared it to sell a clinical test used to aid in the diagnosis of systemic lupus erythematosus, or lupus.</p>
<p>The test detects and measures antibodies to DNA in the blood, they said.</p>
<p>Carl Franzblau, president of Hemagen, said the DNA test, an enzyme immunoassay, completes the company's core line of rheumatology tests produced in the ELISA format.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859 1610</p>
</text>
